lib: create the module directory in install-exec-hook

install-exec-hook starts with an unconditional
cd $(DESTDIR)$(gensiolibexecdir), where

  gensiolibexecdir = $(moduleinstalldir)/$(PACKAGE_VERSION)
  moduleinstalldir = $(pkglibexecdir)
  pkglibexecdir    = $(libexecdir)/gensio

That directory is only ever created as a side effect of installing the
dynamic module libraries.  A build that folds every gensio into the main
library - Freetz configures with --with-all-gensios=yes, which is the
same as --with-<gensio>=yes for every gensio - produces no modules at
all, so nothing creates the directory and the cd fails, aborting the
install:

  make  install-exec-hook
  /bin/bash: line 1: cd: .../usr/local/libexec/gensio/2.8.15: \
      No such file or directory
  make: *** [Makefile:2275: install-am] Error 2

The two rm -f commands that follow are no-ops in that configuration
anyway, because $(gensiolibexec_LTLIBRARIES) is empty - only the cd is
fatal.

Create the directory with automake's own portable mkdir -p first.  That
keeps this to one added line and leaves the two existing commands, and
their individual exit statuses, alone.  Guarding them with "test -d"
instead would collapse them into a single shell block whose status is
that of the last command, so a failure to remove
$(gensiolibexec_LTLIBRARIES) would go unreported.  The cost is an empty
$(libexecdir)/gensio/$(PACKAGE_VERSION) left behind by a module-less
install; in the normal module-ful case the new line is a no-op on a
directory libtool has already created.

lib/Makefile.in is not touched upstream, being generated by
./reconf / automake.  It is shipped in the release tarball, and Freetz
only runs ./configure, so it carries the same hunk here.

uninstall-hook has the same unconditional cd and the same latent bug;
left alone to keep the change to one concern.

Upstream: https://github.com/cminyard/gensio/pull/102

--- lib/Makefile.am
+++ lib/Makefile.am
@@ -449,6 +449,7 @@
 endif
 
 install-exec-hook:
+	@$(MKDIR_P) "$(DESTDIR)$(gensiolibexecdir)"
 	@(cd $(DESTDIR)$(gensiolibexecdir) && $(RM) -f $(gensiolibexec_LTLIBRARIES))
 	@(cd $(DESTDIR)$(gensiolibexecdir) && $(RM) -f $(xgensio_libs))
 
--- lib/Makefile.in
+++ lib/Makefile.in
@@ -2574,6 +2574,7 @@
 .PHONY gensiolibexec-dummyprereq:
 
 install-exec-hook:
+	@$(MKDIR_P) "$(DESTDIR)$(gensiolibexecdir)"
 	@(cd $(DESTDIR)$(gensiolibexecdir) && $(RM) -f $(gensiolibexec_LTLIBRARIES))
 	@(cd $(DESTDIR)$(gensiolibexecdir) && $(RM) -f $(xgensio_libs))
 
